Present without VSync on request: ORION2RE_NO_VSYNC=1 ("the start hang").

STATUS: APPLIED 26 September 2026 by work order 175 on Data's
authorisation — orion2re orionlayer-local f98b8547, rebuilt, bundle
~/orion2re_bundle_26sep_cc542e02.bundle. Written by work order 174 part
A (doc/briefs/174-progress.md), open fix 31. Before the apply: What was shown: the patch applies to src/game/platform.cpp at
orion2re e6199966 (`patch -p1 --dry-run` in the tree); a scratch copy of
e6199966 (`git archive` plus the vendors folder) built with it under the
linux-debug settings (Ninja, Debug, ORION2RE_EXT=ON) and RAN: with
ORION2RE_NO_VSYNC=1, 48 of 50 starts reached "ext: server started" with
none in the start hang (the two others were not caught hanging; 30 more
starts with a backtrace armed were all ready); the same scratch build
without it hung in 1 of 20, Data's own build in 8 of 60 counted starts.

WHY: platform.cpp turns VSync on (SDL_SetRenderVSync(..., 1), lines 644
and 1390), so every present waits for the display. When the compositor
does not draw the window - the screen locked or blanked, or the window
fully covered (26 September: a full-screen game) - a present can wait
forever: backtraces show the main thread in the NVIDIA GLX swap
(drmSyncobjTimelineWait; with __NV_DISABLE_EXPLICIT_SYNC=1 in
xcb_wait_for_special_event instead; with SDL_RENDER_DRIVER=vulkan in
VULKAN_AcquireNextSwapchainImage), and the game thread in
video::Submit_Palette_ / video::Publish_Off_Page_, waiting for that
present with no timeout (SDL_WaitCondition, timeoutNS=-1) - inside
JIM::Draw_Logos_, right after "mox2: data space allocated". The default
does not change; only a run that sets the variable presents without
waiting.

diff --git a/src/game/platform.cpp b/src/game/platform.cpp
index 8e6d8e0..399f958 100644
--- a/src/game/platform.cpp
+++ b/src/game/platform.cpp
@@ -10,6 +10,20 @@ uint32_t g_last_scan_code;
 
 namespace platform {
 	namespace {
+#ifdef ORION2RE_EXT
+		// ORION2RE_NO_VSYNC=1: present without waiting for the display.
+		// A VSync present to a window the compositor is not drawing
+		// (screen locked or blanked, window fully covered) never
+		// completes, and the game thread waits for it without a timeout
+		// (video::Submit_Palette_, video::Publish_Off_Page_): the start
+		// hangs in its first logo frames. Unattended runs set this.
+		int Present_VSync_Interval_() {
+			const char* value = SDL_getenv("ORION2RE_NO_VSYNC");
+			return (value != nullptr && value[0] != '\0' && value[0] != '0') ? 0 : 1;
+		}
+#else
+		int Present_VSync_Interval_() { return 1; }
+#endif
 		bool g_has_lost_focus;
 		SDL_Window* g_sdl_window;
 		SDL_Renderer* g_sdl_renderer;
@@ -641,7 +655,7 @@ namespace platform {
 
 				// Match the original frame-present cadence more closely by blocking on
 				// display refresh when the active renderer backend supports it.
-				(void)SDL_SetRenderVSync(g_sdl_renderer, 1);
+				(void)SDL_SetRenderVSync(g_sdl_renderer, Present_VSync_Interval_());
 			}
 
 			if (!Ensure_Render_Presentation_()) {
@@ -1387,7 +1401,7 @@ namespace platform {
 			SDL_Quit();
 			return 0;
 		}
-		(void)SDL_SetRenderVSync(g_sdl_renderer, 1);
+		(void)SDL_SetRenderVSync(g_sdl_renderer, Present_VSync_Interval_());
 #ifdef ORION2RE_EXT
 		if (!ext::g_hide_window)
 #endif
